<section class="panel media-panel">
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <ul class="plain-list">
        <li>Pick a playlist and the player swaps <code>list=</code>, so YouTube handles the queue.</li>
        <li>Use YouTube's own next, previous, shuffle, fullscreen and volume controls, the same as on youtube.com.</li>
        <li>Want just one video? Open any playlist on YouTube, copy the video URL, and replace the iframe <code>src</code> with <code>https://www.youtube.com/embed/VIDEO_ID</code>.</li>
        <li>All (195) is the jukebox. Classic, Wrath and TBC are the era picks our readers ask for most.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="meta-info">If a playlist shows empty, the channel may have made it private, so pick All or Classic as a fallback. Nothing is stored on our side beyond the playlist you last chose.</p>
